WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.217
Hi, I'm Jib!

00:00:02.217 --> 00:00:05.614
NVIDIA's new small model talks, calls tools and drives a robot.

00:00:05.614 --> 00:00:09.320
Why does a four gig model ship as a six gig file?

00:00:10.767 --> 00:00:14.857
Bolt keeps Gemma's architecture and retrains the text weights with reinforcement learning.

00:00:14.857 --> 00:00:18.606
Its biggest table is only looked up, so it can stay

00:00:18.606 --> 00:00:19.969
out of graphics memory.

00:00:21.525 --> 00:00:22.995
No supervised stage at all.

00:00:23.836 --> 00:00:25.856
Start from Google's Gemma, unchanged.

00:00:26.323 --> 00:00:29.262
Train every prompt with thinking on and off, mostly off.

00:00:29.682 --> 00:00:32.831
Penalise long answers, in cycles, so the voice stays short.

00:00:33.251 --> 00:00:34.793
Then quantize to four bits.

00:00:36.675 --> 00:00:40.337
A token becomes an embedding and climbs forty two decoder layers.

00:00:40.757 --> 00:00:44.374
Gemma's small models add a second table: a small vector per

00:00:44.374 --> 00:00:45.689
token, for every layer.

00:00:46.109 --> 00:00:48.217
The token id just picks one row.

00:00:48.217 --> 00:00:50.024
A lookup, not a matrix multiply.

00:00:50.444 --> 00:00:52.975
Each layer gates its slice and adds it in.

00:00:52.975 --> 00:00:55.224
So the table can live in ordinary memory.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:00.573
In the four bit file, the computing parts come to about three

00:01:00.573 --> 00:01:01.831
point one seven gigabytes.

00:01:01.831 --> 00:01:04.976
The lookup table is another three, kept on the CPU.

00:01:06.625 --> 00:01:09.103
Every sixth layer attends to the whole context.

00:01:09.103 --> 00:01:11.271
Those are the layers whose cache grows.

00:01:11.691 --> 00:01:15.493
The last eighteen layers borrow keys and values from earlier ones, so

00:01:15.493 --> 00:01:17.394
only twenty four keep a cache.

00:01:18.758 --> 00:01:21.478
Bolt gains a lot on instructions and personas.

00:01:21.478 --> 00:01:25.559
On long multi turn tool tasks, Qwen still leads by twenty points.

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:28.770
So the four gigabytes is graphics memory.

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:31.513
The lookup table is the other half of the file.

00:01:34.942 --> 00:01:36.035
Gemma's skeleton, retrained.

00:01:36.035 --> 00:01:37.857
A table on the CPU.

00:01:37.857 --> 00:01:40.407
A cache only twenty four layers deep.

00:01:40.827 --> 00:01:42.849
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:42.849 --> 00:01:43.427
I'm Jib.

00:01:43.427 --> 00:01:43.716
Bye!
